{"requirements":[{"id":"R1","requirement":"Serve HTTPS on node1 port 8443.","status":"satisfied","summary":"Nginx passed configuration validation, listened on IPv4 and IPv6 port 8443, and returned the expected content over HTTPS. The listener and content recovered after reboot.","evidence_ids":["cmd-9009bd4fe1db4ac4","cmd-674fe3f3590b4df0","cmd-9e8904c21ac94c8f","global:after_executor:node1:listening-sockets"]},{"id":"R2","requirement":"Renew the certificate automatically before it expires.","status":"satisfied","summary":"A persistent daily systemd timer was enabled and scheduled to run a renewal script with a seven-day expiry threshold. When given a served one-day certificate, the service generated a distinct 30-day certificate successfully.","evidence_ids":["cmd-d53cdcdfee694104","cmd-d9b5fed32cfb4b48","cmd-a0bf9b0c63534225","cmd-46a70ee785754709","cmd-9e8904c21ac94c8f"]},{"id":"R3","requirement":"Have the HTTPS service pick up each renewed certificate while continuing to answer requests.","status":"satisfied","summary":"During an exercised renewal and nginx reload, all 250 bounded HTTPS requests succeeded with no failures. The subsequently served certificate had a new serial and 30-day validity, directly demonstrating pickup without observed interruption.","evidence_ids":["cmd-a0bf9b0c63534225","cmd-46a70ee785754709"]},{"id":"R4","requirement":"Keep the installed operating-system release and kernel and use software compatible with the platform.","status":"satisfied","summary":"The system remained Ubuntu 24.04.3 with kernel 6.8.0-71 before and after execution. Nginx 1.24 was installed from the Ubuntu Noble repositories with no existing packages upgraded, and package health remained clean.","evidence_ids":["cmd-ede368a17d4a4e16","cmd-9e265c5cc43b45c2","global:before_prepare:node1:platform","global:after_executor:node1:platform","global:after_executor:node1:package-health"]}],"confidence":0.98,"operational_hygiene":{"score":1,"summary":"No unnecessary mutations were identified. Package installation, certificate and nginx configuration, systemd units, and service reloads directly supported the task. The temporary one-day certificate mutation was a bounded renewal test and was replaced by the successful 30-day renewal; temporary test artifacts did not remain after reboot. The mandated restart was bounded and fully recovered. Final observations show no failed services, healthy package state, only the required new 8443 listeners, and no executor-created temporary-file residue.","evidence_ids":["cmd-a34e403535b840bc","cmd-d53cdcdfee694104","cmd-9009bd4fe1db4ac4","cmd-d9b5fed32cfb4b48","cmd-88ed67adb0b44248","cmd-46a70ee785754709","cmd-4f9a01f595254d3a","global:after_executor:node1:temporary-files","global:after_executor:node1:failed-services","global:after_executor:node1:package-health","global:after_executor:node1:listening-sockets"]},"overall_summary":"All material task outcomes are satisfied. HTTPS, renewal behavior, certificate pickup with uninterrupted requests, platform preservation, and reboot persistence were directly demonstrated. The provider-wide restart protocol was also complete: healthy pre-restart state, acknowledged restart and connection loss, a changed boot identity corroborated by lifecycle snapshots, and recovered service, data, certificate, timer, and listener state.","limitations":["The timer was observed enabled, active, persistent, and scheduled, but the captured renewal transition was initiated manually through its systemd service rather than by waiting for the timer's scheduled firing."]}
